.\" icdu.1 - the manual page of icdu. Written by hand, in the layout of ncdu's page.
.\" A test (args::tests::man_page_lists_the_same_options) compares its options with the
.\" program's.
.TH ICDU 1 "2026-11-17" "icdu" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
icdu \- disk usage explorer that can be browsed and searched while it scans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B icdu
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B icdu
shows where the space on a disk has gone: a list of the entries of a directory, largest
first, that can be walked through, sorted, searched and cleaned up.
.PP
It does not wait for the scan to finish.
The list is on screen at once, sizes fill in and add up while the scan runs, and the
directory that is being looked at is scanned next.
.B /
searches the whole tree by name, including what the scan has only just reached.
.PP
icdu is compatible with
.BR ncdu (1):
it has ncdu's keys and options, reads ncdu's configuration files, and reads and writes
ncdu's JSON export format.
Where it differs is listed under
.BR "DIFFERENCES FROM NCDU" .
.PP
Without a
.IR directory ,
the current one is scanned.
.SH OPTIONS
Short options can be bundled
.RB ( \-xe ),
and a value can be attached to its option or follow it
.RB ( \-o\- ,
.BR "\-o file" ,
.BR \-\-exclude=tmp ,
.BR "\-\-exclude tmp" ).
.B \-\-
ends the options.
Of two options that contradict each other the later one wins; every option that switches
something has a counterpart that switches it back.
.SS Mode selection
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and keys, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Browse a tree from an export file instead of scanning.
.B \-
reads standard input.
The file is not the local filesystem: delete, shell, open and rescan are off.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Scan, write the tree to
.I FILE
in ncdu's JSON format, and exit without opening the browser.
.B \-
writes to standard output.
With
.B \-f
this converts a dump.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extended ", " \-\-no\-extended
Also record owner, group, mode and modification time of every entry.
They are shown by
.B m
and
.BR i ,
can be sorted by with
.BR M ,
and are written to and read from export files.
As in ncdu the option has to be given when reading such a file as well.
It costs 32 bytes of memory per entry.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-config
Do not read the configuration files.
.SS Scan options
These have no effect with
.BR \-f .
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-one\-file\-system ", " \-\-cross\-file\-system
Do not enter directories on other filesystems than the one the scan started on.
They are listed, flagged
.BR > ,
and not counted.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " \fIPATTERN\fR"
Leave out entries that match the shell pattern.
The pattern is tried against the whole path of an entry and against every tail of the path
that starts after a slash, so
.B node_modules
excludes every entry of that name,
.B src/build
only a
.B build
inside a
.BR src ,
and
.B /var/cache
that directory.
.B *
and
.B ?
also match a slash.
Can be given several times.
Excluded entries are listed, flagged
.BR < ,
neither entered nor counted.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-exclude\-from " \fIFILE\fR"
Read patterns from
.IR FILE ,
one per line, each taken as it stands.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-caches ", " \-\-include\-caches
Leave out directories that hold a
.B CACHEDIR.TAG
file with the signature of the Cache Directory Tagging Specification.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-kernfs ", " \-\-include\-kernfs
Leave out the Linux kernel's pseudo filesystems (proc, sysfs, cgroup, debugfs, devpts and
the like), wherever they are mounted.
They are flagged
.BR ^ .
No effect on other systems.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-follow\-symlinks ", " \-\-no\-follow\-symlinks
Count a symlink to a file as that file.
Each such link counts on its own.
Symlinks to directories are never followed.
Deleting such an entry removes the link and not the file.
.TP
.BR \-\-older\-than " \fIDUR\fR, " \-\-newer\-than " \fIDUR\fR"
Leave out entries that were last modified more than, or less than,
.I DUR
ago.
.I DUR
is a number with a unit:
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.BR h ,
.BR d ,
.BR w
or
.BR y ;
without a unit, days.
Not in ncdu.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
The number of threads that read directories.
The default is four per processor core, at least 4 and at most 64.
Fewer are better on a single spinning disk.
.SS Export options
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-1 ", " \-2
What to show while scanning:
nothing
.RB ( \-0 ,
the default with
.BR "\-o \-" ),
one line of progress
.RB ( \-1 ,
the default with
.BR "\-o \fIFILE\fR" ),
or the browser
.RB ( \-2 ,
the default otherwise).
.B \-0
and
.B \-1
without
.B \-o
scan first and open the browser afterwards.
.SS Interface options
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-slow\-ui\-updates ", " \-\-fast\-ui\-updates
Redraw the screen every two seconds while scanning instead of ten times a second.
Useful over a slow remote connection.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-read\-only
Turn the delete key off.
Given twice
.RB ( \-rr ),
also the shell, the opener and the export key: nothing is left that changes the filesystem
or runs a program.
.TP
.BR \-\-disable\-delete ", " \-\-enable\-delete
Turn the delete key
.RB ( d )
off, or on.
.TP
.BR \-\-disable\-shell ", " \-\-enable\-shell
Turn the shell
.RB ( b )
and the opener
.RB ( o )
off, or on.
.TP
.BR \-\-disable\-refresh ", " \-\-enable\-refresh
Turn rescanning
.RB ( r )
off, or on.
.TP
.BR \-\-delete\-command " \fICMD\fR"
Delete by running
.I CMD
instead of removing the entry.
The command is run by
.B /bin/sh
with the path of the entry as its last argument and in the variable
.BR NCDU_DELETE_PATH ,
with the terminal, in the directory icdu was started in.
Afterwards icdu looks at what is left.
For example
.B "\-\-delete\-command 'gio trash \-\-'"
or
.BR "\-\-delete\-command 'rm \-ri \-\-'" .
.TP
.BR \-\-confirm\-quit ", " \-\-no\-confirm\-quit
Ask before quitting.
.TP
.BR \-\-confirm\-delete ", " \-\-no\-confirm\-delete
Ask before deleting (the default), or do not.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-apparent\-size ", " \-\-disk\-usage
Show the apparent sizes of files instead of the space they take on disk.
.TP
.BR \-\-si ", " \-\-no\-si
Show sizes in powers of 1000 (kB, MB, GB) instead of 1024 (KiB, MiB, GiB).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " \fISCHEME\fR"
.BR off ,
.B dark
or
.BR dark\-bg .
Colours are on unless the environment variable
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
icdu has one colour scheme, for which both of ncdu's names stand.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-hidden ", " \-\-hide\-hidden
List entries whose name starts with a dot and excluded entries, or do not.
Hidden entries are still counted.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-graph ", " \-\-hide\-graph
Show the bar that compares each entry with the largest one, or do not.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-percent ", " \-\-hide\-percent
Show each entry's share of its directory, or do not.
.TP
.BR \-\-graph\-style " \fISTYLE\fR"
Draw the bar with
.B hash
characters, or with block characters to half a cell
.RB ( half\-block )
or to an eighth
.RB ( eighth\-block ).
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-itemcount ", " \-\-hide\-itemcount
Show the number of entries below each directory, or do not.
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-mtime ", " \-\-hide\-mtime
Show the modification time, for a directory the latest one below it, or do not.
Needs
.BR \-e .
.TP
.BR \-\-sort " \fICOLUMN\fR"
Sort by
.B disk\-usage
(the default),
.BR apparent\-size ,
.BR name ,
.B itemcount
or
.BR mtime .
.B \-asc
or
.B \-desc
after the name sets the direction, as in
.BR \-\-sort=name\-desc .
.TP
.BR \-\-group\-directories\-first ", " \-\-no\-group\-directories\-first
List directories before everything else.
.TP
.BR \-\-disable\-natsort ", " \-\-enable\-natsort
Order names byte by byte.
By default a run of digits counts as the number it spells, so that
.B file2
comes before
.BR file10 .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Default options are read from configuration files, one option per line, written as on the
command line, with the value of an option after it on the same line and taken as it stands.
Lines that start with
.B #
and empty lines are ignored.
A line that starts with
.B @
may fail without that being an error.
In the file name of
.BR \-X ,
.B ~/
is the home directory.
.PP
Four files are read, each overriding the ones before it, and the command line overrides
them all:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/etc/ncdu.conf
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ncdu/config    (~/.config/ncdu/config)
/etc/icdu.conf
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/icdu/config    (~/.config/icdu/config)
.fi
.RE
.PP
The first two are ncdu's own, so that a setup made for ncdu applies.
What icdu cannot use in them is reported and passed over.
A mistake in one of icdu's own files is an error.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Always record owner, mode and time
\-e
# Leave out .git directories
\-\-exclude .git
# This file need not exist
@\-\-exclude\-from ~/.ncduexcludes
.fi
.RE
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B ?
Help.
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " down ", " up
Move the selection.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Ctrl\-U ", " Ctrl\-D
Move by a page.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End ", " G
Jump to the first or the last entry.
.TP
.BR l ", " Enter ", " right
Enter the selected directory.
.TP
.BR h ", " < ", " Backspace ", " left
Go to the parent directory.
.TP
.B /
Search by name in the whole tree.
Matches are listed as the query is typed, largest first.
.B Enter
goes to the selected one,
.B Tab
limits the search to the directory on screen,
.B Esc
closes it.
.TP
.BR ] ", " [
Go to the next or the previous match of the last search.
.TP
.BR s ", " n ", " C ", " M
Sort by size, name, item count or modification time.
The key of the active column reverses the order.
.B M
needs
.BR \-e .
.TP
.B t
Directories before files, or not.
.TP
.B a
Switch between disk usage and apparent size.
.TP
.B e
Show or hide hidden and excluded entries.
.TP
.B g
Bar and percentage: both, neither, the bar, the percentage.
.TP
.B c
Show or hide the item counts.
.TP
.B m
Show or hide the modification times.
Needs
.BR \-e .
.TP
.B i
Details of the selected entry.
.TP
.B T
The largest files below the directory on screen.
Not in ncdu.
.TP
.BR x ", " !
Jump to the next entry that could not be read.
Not in ncdu.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected entry, after a question.
A directory can only be deleted when all of it has been scanned.
.TP
.B r
Scan the directory on screen again.
.TP
.B b
Start a shell in the directory on screen.
.TP
.B o
Open the selected entry with the system's default application.
Not in ncdu.
.TP
.B E
Write the tree to
.B icdu\-dump.json
in the current directory, in the export format.
Not in ncdu.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-L ", " Ctrl\-Z
Redraw the screen; suspend icdu.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.SH FILE FLAGS
Each row starts with a flag:
.TP
.B !
The directory or entry could not be read.
.TP
.B .
Something further down could not be read, so the size may be too small.
.TP
.B <
Excluded: by a pattern, as a cache directory, or by the time filters.
.TP
.B >
A directory on another filesystem
.RB ( \-x ).
.TP
.B ^
A kernel filesystem
.RB ( \-\-exclude\-kernfs ).
.TP
.B H
A hard link whose file is counted at another of its names.
.TP
.B @
Neither a file nor a directory: a symlink, device, socket or fifo.
.TP
.B e
An empty directory.
.TP
.B F
A firmlink (only in export files written by ncdu on macOS).
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan and browse the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.B icdu
.RE
.PP
A whole filesystem, without what is mounted below it:
.PP
.RS
.B "icdu \-x /"
.RE
.PP
Scan now, look later:
.PP
.RS
.nf
.B "icdu \-1xo\- / | gzip > export.gz"
.B "zcat export.gz | icdu \-f\-"
.fi
.RE
.PP
From a cron job, use
.B \-0
in place of
.B \-1
to keep it silent.
.PP
Scan a remote machine and browse the result here.
ncdu on the remote side works as well as icdu:
.PP
.RS
.B "ssh \-C user@host icdu \-o\- / | icdu \-f\-"
.RE
.PP
Move to the trash instead of deleting:
.PP
.RS
.B "icdu \-\-delete\-command 'gio trash \-\-'"
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCDU_SHELL
The command the shell key runs, in place of
.BR SHELL .
Without either,
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B NCDU_LEVEL
Set to 1 in the shell that icdu starts, or to one more than icdu itself was started with.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, icdu starts without colours.
.TP
.BR HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the configuration files are looked for.
.SH SIGNALS
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGHUP ", " SIGINT " and " SIGQUIT
end icdu.
The browser first gives the terminal back (line mode, the screen that was there before, the
cursor) and then ends by the same signal.
That takes a fraction of a second, and about a second if icdu is busy or the terminal is not
taking output.
Closing the terminal ends icdu as well, with or without a hang-up signal.
.PP
.B Ctrl\-Z
gives the terminal back and stops icdu, and
.B SIGCONT
brings the browser back.
Where no shell is above icdu that could continue it, as when icdu is the command a terminal
was started with, the system does not stop it, and icdu says so.
.B SIGTSTP
from outside stops icdu as it is, like
.BR SIGSTOP ;
the screen is set up again when icdu is continued.
.PP
While a shell or the delete command has the terminal,
.BR SIGTERM " and " SIGHUP
end icdu at once.
.BR Ctrl\-C " and " Ctrl\-\e
typed there are for that command and do not end icdu.
.PP
Without the browser
.RB ( \-o ),
every signal has its default effect, also
.B SIGPIPE
when nobody reads the output any more.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the command line or a configuration file is wrong, a scan, an export or an
import fails, or the browser has no terminal.
Ended by a signal, icdu reports that signal and no status of its own.
.SH HARD LINKS
A file with several names is counted once: at the first of its names that the scan comes
across.
The other names are listed with their size, flagged
.BR H ,
and add nothing to any total.
When the counted name is deleted and another one is still in the tree, the size moves to
that one.
.SH DIFFERENCES FROM NCDU
.SS What icdu adds
The browser while the scan runs, the search
.RB ( / ,
.BR ] ,
.BR [ ),
the largest files
.RB ( T ),
the jump to the next read error
.RB ( x ),
opening an entry
.RB ( o ),
the export from the browser
.RB ( E ),
and the time filters
.RB ( \-\-older\-than ,
.BR \-\-newer\-than ).
.SS What icdu does not have
The binary export format of ncdu 2 and its compression:
.BR \-O ,
.BR \-c ,
.BR \-\-compress ,
.BR \-\-no\-compress ,
.B \-\-compress\-level
and
.B \-\-export\-block\-size
are refused, and such files cannot be read.
A zstd or gzip compressed JSON export can be piped in:
.BR "zstd \-dc FILE | icdu \-f\-" .
.PP
The column for sizes shared through hard links
.RB ( u ,
.BR \-\-shared\-column ).
The option is accepted and ignored.
.SS What is different
Times are shown in UTC.
.PP
Bar and percentage are both shown by default; ncdu shows the bar only.
.PP
The scan uses many threads by default
.RB ( \-t );
ncdu 2 uses one.
.PP
Deleting, shell, opening and rescanning are always off for an imported file, also with
.BR \-\-enable\-delete .
.PP
Before an entry is deleted it is checked to be the one that was scanned: same type, device
and inode.
One that has been replaced since stays, and the directory with it.
.PP
A file with several names is counted at one of them (see
.BR "HARD LINKS" ).
ncdu counts it once in every directory that holds one of its names, so the size of a
directory can differ between the two where a file's names lie in different directories.
The total of the scanned directory is the same.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncdu (1),
.BR du (1)
.PP
https://github.com/anhofmann/icdu
